# Close 6 on a1c, partly ideal inputs, S_F kept NORMAL (its head removal BUD-updates F at c1).
# Open state edited by script (order matters: every arming block is placed after the piston it
# arms, and lands next to its quasi cell only, so nothing is updated):
#  * F's killer P_X re-armed: repeater f removed, R_Z off (P_X retracts), R_X back at (1,5,1),
#    R_Z back at (1,6,1);
#  * padding pistons Xa (1,3,1) facing east (armed by R_X through its quasi cell) and Xb (3,3,1)
#    facing south (armed by a block at (3,4,2)), D armed by a block at (4,4,0). FIFO at c1:
#    S_F | F ext (E's neighbors: Xa) | Xa (head into (2,3,1): Xb) | P_X | Xb (base: D) | F ret | D.
#  * R_F is teleported back between c1 and c2 (stands for an early return).
design designs/piston-door-3x3/tracks/fast-clean/a1c-107.txt
probe T 1 2 0
probe C 1 1 0
probe E 1 3 0
probe F 1 4 0
probe D 3 3 0
probe Xa 1 3 1
probe Xb 3 3 1
probe TL 0 2 0
probe TR 2 2 0
probe M 1 0 0
use 0 4 -2
quiet 24
clear 1 6 -1
clear 1 6 1
quiet 4
clear 1 5 2
set 1 3 1 minecraft:piston[facing=east,extended=false]
set 3 3 1 minecraft:piston[facing=south,extended=false]
set 1 5 1 minecraft:redstone_block
set 1 6 1 minecraft:redstone_block
set 3 4 2 minecraft:redstone_block
set 4 4 0 minecraft:redstone_block
quiet 4
plane 0 -4 -2 6 8
print
box -1 -1 -2 4 7 3
mark close
use 0 4 -2
changes 1
clear 2 4 -1
set 1 4 -1 minecraft:redstone_block
trace 9
